  "description": "Optional Indic-script language pack for NetPdf. Registers the major Indic languages (Hindi, Sanskrit, Marathi, Nepali, Bengali, Assamese, Panjabi, Gujarati, Odia, Tamil, Telugu, Kannada, Malayalam) with NetPdf's public HyphenationRegistry so layout can hyphenate a block by its effective lang. Indic scripts DO hyphenate, but this build ships NO pattern data yet — the CTAN hyph-utf8 (LPPL) pattern sets are vendored by the maintainer; until then hyphens:auto produces no breaks for these languages (conservative — never the wrong English hyphenation). Call IndicHyphenation.Register at startup; a module initializer also drives it on assembly load.",
